const BACKSTORY={mags:'Mags: How did I get here? I was repossessing a tankard that owed three months’ rent. It bit me, I bit it back, and we both fell through the bottom of a barrel into this world. The tankard got away. I did not.',
 gulpwell:'Gulpwell: I sold my tavern to a gentleman in a gray coat. He paid in coins that hummed. That night the cellar door opened onto a mountain, and the mountain was here. I kept the coins. They still hum.',
 cumbeard:'Cumbeard: I was trimming my beard in the old world. The scissors slipped, the mirror rippled, and my beard went in first. Where the beard goes, Cumbeard follows. That is the law.',
 splurt:'Splurt: Splurt was wiping table. Table was portal. Splurt wiped too hard. Now Splurt wipes tables here. Same tables. Different world. Better tips.'};
const TALK_LATE={mags:'Mags: When you go home — and you will — check the cellar of that tavern. Professional curiosity.',gulpwell:'Gulpwell: The buyer paid in coins nobody had minted yet. I thought that was a good sign.',cumbeard:'Cumbeard: My beard has a feeling about your old world. It is not a good feeling. It is a tingly one.',splurt:'Splurt: Splurt hear a road home is opening. Splurt pack mop.'};
